      "side": 1,
      "message": "no, I started with including sha256.h, it complains about redefining structures:\n\n```\ninclude/sha256.h:17:8: error: redefinition of \u0027struct sha256_ctx\u0027\n   17 | struct sha256_ctx {\n      |        ^~~~~~~~~~\nIn file included from board/cr50/dcrypto/internal.h:12,\n                 from board/cr50/dcrypto/fips.c:14:\nboard/cr50/dcrypto/dcrypto.h:140:8: note: originally defined here\n  140 | struct sha256_ctx {\n      |        ^~~~~~~~~~\nIn file included from board/cr50/tpm_nvmem_ops.h:10,\n                 from board/cr50/dcrypto/fips.c:22:\n```\n\nincluding \"dcrypto.h\" has different but similar problems:\n```\nIn file included from include/vboot.h:11,\n                 from common/ec_efs.c:24:\ninclude/sha256.h:17:8: error: redefinition of \u0027struct sha256_ctx\u0027\n   17 | struct sha256_ctx {\n      |        ^~~~~~~~~~\nIn file included from board/cr50/tpm_nvmem_ops.h:10,\n                 from common/ec_efs.c:23:\n/mnt/host/source/src/platform/cr50/board/cr50/dcrypto/dcrypto.h:140:8: note: originally defined here\n  140 | struct sha256_ctx {\n      |        ^~~~~~~~~~\nIn file included from include/vboot.h:11,\n                 from common/ec_efs.c:24:\n```\n\nI don\u0027t want to untangle our dependency trees in what is supposed to be a simple quickfix CL. additionally, both sha256.h and dcrypto.h seem to pull too much into context when all we need is a simple size const. so went this #ifndef-define route instead. it\u0027s low risk since the meaning (and value) of SHA256_DIGEST_SIZE is pretty universal across all its uses.",
